[Unit]
Description=freehire worker: safety-net close for boards proven unreachable, or proven empty, for weeks
After=network.target postgresql.service
[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=freehire
WorkingDirectory=/opt/freehire/src/hire-current
EnvironmentFile=/opt/freehire/.env
# Reads board_health and jobs only — a handful of rows even on a bad day, never the crawl
# fleet's own load.
CPUWeight=20
IOWeight=20
# --apply ARMS THE UNREACHABLE PASS. That was the review the dry-run default was waiting
# for, and it is recorded here rather than in a commit message nobody will find:
#
#   * The report was read on 2026-09-17. It offered 94 boards and 6,637 postings — down
#     from 353 and 20,106 the day before, because 325 of those records were stale
#     case-duplicates of boards crawling normally, which migration 0170 removed and
#     ListChronicBoards now refuses (freehire#2950). Arming the worker on the earlier
#     number would have closed live boards' postings under the label board_unreachable.
#   * The survivors were probed against the live platforms, not taken from last_error,
#     which is 60+ days old by construction: 12 of 12 sampled ashby boards answer 404
#     today, and the bamboohr cluster — reported as "decode invalid" rather than gone —
#     302-redirects a dead tenant to bamboohr.com's marketing page, which is the vendor
#     saying the account is closed.
#   * The counts now also reach the node_exporter textfile collector
#     (freehire_chronic_board_jobs, and _armed beside it), because the journal rotates
#     inside a day and six days of these reports were already lost unread.
#
# --apply-empty-feed is deliberately still ABSENT, and adding one flag must not be read as
# endorsing the other: --apply arms the unreachable pass, --apply-empty-feed arms the
# empty-feed pass (migration 0158), and each reports its own boards for its own reasons.
# Reviewing "no board could be reached" evidence says nothing about whether the boards
# reported as EMPTY are really empty — that pass currently offers 1 board and 2 postings,
# and nobody has checked them.
ExecStart=/opt/freehire/src/hire-current/close-chronic-boards --apply
